			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for Sky diagnostic bridge refinement\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from `8fe235bf` to `1a736c21` to revert brittle forced-initialization logic in the diagnostic bridge and align with the reactive data-driven model.\n\nThe update syncs the Sky submodule to replace the previous implementation in `InstallDiagnostics.ts`, which forcibly opened the Problems panel on every diagnostic batch. This change removes all `openView` calls, throttling mechanisms, and per-batch visibility checks.\n\nThe new implementation relies on `IMarkerService.changeOne` for state updates and allows `MarkersView` to manage visibility naturally. A single, one-time intervention is introduced to clear persisted `activeFile` filters if the panel is already visible upon diagnostic arrival. This resolves the \"count shows but panel empty\" issue caused by stale filters without forcing UI state changes.\n\nThese updates reduce IPC overhead, eliminate unnecessary side effects, and ensure diagnostic updates strictly follow the reactive lifecycle of the editor UI.",
			"SHA": "0035fccf8743954dd5d67dda3331b22b7bd7a28b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T08:01:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for stability refinements\n\nUpdate the `Element` git submodule from `deb49bcb` to `8fe235bf` to apply targeted stability fixes within the editor ecosystem.\n\nThis sync follows the previous major IPC alignment and error propagation update, addressing residual issues in the extension host (Cocoon) and native backend (Mountain) to ensure consistent behavior during extension loading and file system operations.\n\nSpecific changes include:\n- **Cocoon:** Refine task scheduling logic to prevent race conditions during the initialization of new language server protocols.\n- **Mountain:** Correct a minor edge case in `CacheBlob` serialization that could lead to transient state mismatches under high-load file system activity.\n- **Sky:** Optimize the cleanup of temporary webview containers to reduce memory pressure during rapid view switching.\n\nThese updates further solidify the IPC contract and ensure a stable runtime environment for the extension host and UI layers.",
			"SHA": "0898e1fa5d0437ca21b7928be8a302ccc0e96132"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T07:59:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for IPC alignment and error propagation\n\nUpdate the Element git submodule from `bab9e25f` to `deb49bcb` to enforce strict PascalCase IPC contracts, restore error propagation, and eliminate event loop instability across the editor ecosystem.\n\nKey changes across the element tree include:\n- **Cocoon:** Refactor all RPC method invocations to strictly match `Vine.proto` PascalCase definitions (e.g., `Window.ShowMessage`, `FileSystem.Stat`) to prevent silent gRPC rejections. Standardize task types and workspace save fallbacks.\n- **Mountain:** Fix `build.rs` to generate valid `CacheBlob` JSON structs. Shift `WindServiceHandlers` to propagate I/O and path resolution errors instead of swallowing them, preventing silent document conflicts. Implement missing handlers for `Storage.GetItems`, `tree.reveal`, and `showTextDocument`.\n- **Output:** Reorder imports in compiled `Accessor.js` artifacts to align with TypeScript definition pattern matching rules, preventing structural drift.\n- **Sky:** Consolidate duplicate `onDidChangeActiveCodeEditor` listeners to prevent double-firing. Implement retry logic with exponential backoff for SCM group registration. Correct inline completion logic to avoid wrapping non-snippet text. Fix missing `@tauri-apps/api/core` imports.\n- **Wind:** Register new IPC channels for Language features, Tree Views, and Model updates. Correct the `createWorker` stub to return a direct `Promise` to resolve deadlocks in the `DiskFileSystemProvider` worker lifecycle.\n\nThese updates ensure robust IPC communication, accurate error handling in the native backend, and stable event routing between the extension host and UI layers.",
			"SHA": "99b929abbb61a64325dd2848cc54756209180ebc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T07:06:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodule for custom editor resolver alignment\n\nUpdate the `Element` git submodule to `bab9e25f` to enable end-to-end support for custom editor contributions (e.g., Markdown previews, image viewers) defined in extension manifests.\n\nKey changes across the editor element tree include:\n- **Cocoon:** Enhance `RegisterCustomEditor` to extract and transmit the file `Selector` (glob patterns) alongside `ViewType` and `Options`, ensuring Mountain receives the full registration contract required to route file opens correctly.\n- **Output:** Expose `IEditorResolverService` and `RegisteredEditorPriority` constants via the `ExposeAccessor` interface, allowing the extension host to programmatically register and prioritize custom editors.\n- **Sky:** Refactor `InstallWebview` payload parsing to support named-key arguments (`viewType`, `options`, `selector`), replacing legacy positional assumptions. Integrate `IEditorResolverService` registration with a `priority.option` fallback to ensure activation events fire reliably during lazy extension loading.\n\nThese updates ensure custom editors are correctly registered, file associations are honored, and the resolver service is available across the Mountain-Cocoon-Sky IPC boundary.",
			"SHA": "c6065c43f3264fd54c508b350f4b3997fdd82f09"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T06:29:02Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				133,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Element submodules to resolve UTF-8 path handling and extension host races\n\nUpdate the `Element` git submodule from `3d955d1a` to `e3694627` to address race conditions in the extension host and repair binary/UTF-8 integrity in the native IPC layer.\n\nKey changes across the editor element tree include:\n- **Cocoon:** Reorder bootstrap sequence to initialize `ModuleInterceptor` before `MountainConnection`, preventing startup race conditions. Relax `IsValidMethod` regex to support dynamic LSP methods (e.g., `$onDid*`) and normalize diagnostic shapes to prevent silent marker drops.\n- **Mountain:** Standardize DTO naming to PascalCase and rewrite `percent_decode` in `PathExtraction` to correctly reconstruct multi-byte UTF-8 sequences, resolving ENOENT errors on international file paths. Repair `FileWriteNative` to handle base64 buffers.\n- **Sky:** Eliminate double-dispatch in bridge relays and fix the \"count shows but panel empty\" issue in the Problems view by throttling `ViewsSvc.openView` calls and persistently clearing active file filters.\n- **Wind:** Define new IPC channels for Git operations (`GitExec`, `GitClone`) and SCM provider activation to enable integrated version control workflows.\n\nThese updates ensure robust binary data integrity, correct handling of non-ASCII paths, stable event routing, and reliable diagnostic visibility across the extension host and UI layers.",
			"SHA": "54b87fa66bfd8ff4513504c90f8d5b2d664162e6"
		}
	],
